.SH "NAME"
econf\&.ReadDirsHistory, econf\&.ReadDirsHistoryWithCallback \- evaluate every configuration file found in two directories, unmerged

.SH "SYNOPSIS"

.sp
.ft B
.nf
import "github\&.com/openSUSE/libeconf/go/econf"
.fi
.ft
.sp
.nf
\fBfunc ReadDirsHistory(usrConfDir, etcConfDir, configName, configSuffix, delim, comment string) ([]*econf\&.File, error)\fR

\fBfunc ReadDirsHistoryWithCallback(usrConfDir, etcConfDir, configName, configSuffix, delim, comment string, callback econf\&.FileCallback) ([]*econf\&.File, error)\fR
.fi

.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.PP
\fBReadDirsHistory\fR
evaluates key/values for every configuration file found in
\fIusrConfDir\fR
(normally
"/usr/etc"
) and
\fIetcConfDir\fR
(normally
"/etc"
) and returns one
\fI*econf\&.File\fR
per file found, in the order they were read (lowest to highest
precedence)\&. Unlike
\fBReadConfig\fR
(see
\fBeconf_go_ReadConfig\fR(3)), the individual files are
\fBnot\fR
merged into a single result\&.

.PP
The
\fIconfigName\fR
parameter is the basename of the configuration file\&.
\fIconfigSuffix\fR
is the suffix of the configuration file, and may be
""\&.
The
\fIdelim\fR
parameter specifies the character(s) used to separate keys from values\&.
If
\fIdelim\fR
contains space characters AND non\-space characters, multiline values are
not parseable\&. The
\fIcomment\fR
parameter specifies an array of characters which define the start of a
comment\&.

.PP
\fBReadDirsHistoryWithCallback\fR
behaves like
\fBReadDirsHistory\fR, additionally invoking
\fIcallback\fR
(see
\fBeconf_go_FileCallback\fR(3)) for every candidate file before it is
parsed\&. Returning
\fIfalse\fR
from
\fIcallback\fR
aborts the read, and the call fails with
\fBeconf\&.ErrParsingCallbackFailed\fR\&.

.PP
Each
\fI*File\fR
in the returned slice should be released with
\fB(*File)\&.Close\fR
(see
\fBeconf_go_File_Close\fR(3)) once it is no longer needed\&.

.SH "RETURN VALUE"

.PP
On success, these functions return a non\-nil slice of
\fI*econf\&.File\fR
and a
\fInil\fR
error\&. The slice is
\fInil\fR
if no matching file was found\&.

.PP
On failure, they return
\fInil\fR
and a non\-nil
\fI*econf\&.Error\fR
(see
\fBeconf_go_Error\fR(3))\&.

.SH "ERRORS"

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrNoMem\fR
.RS 4
          Insufficient memory to allocate the resulting list of
\fBeconf\&.File\fR
objects\&.
.RE

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrMissingBracket\fR, \fBeconf\&.ErrTextAfterSection\fR, \fBeconf\&.ErrEmptySectionName\fR, \fBeconf\&.ErrMissingDelimiter\fR
.RS 4
          A file contains syntax errors and could not be parsed successfully\&.
.RE

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrArgumentIsNullValue\fR
.RS 4
          One of the required arguments is empty when it must not be\&.
.RE

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrParsingCallbackFailed\fR
.RS 4
          \fBReadDirsHistoryWithCallback\fR
only: the callback returned
\fIfalse\fR
for one of the candidate files\&.
.RE

.SH "EXAMPLE"
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 1
.\}
.nf

package main

import (
    "log"

    "github\&.com/openSUSE/libeconf/go/econf"
)

func main() {
    files, err := econf\&.ReadDirsHistory(
        "/usr/etc", "/etc", "example", "conf", "=", "#")
    if err != nil {
        log\&.Fatal(err)
    }
    for _, f := range files {
        log\&.Println(f\&.Path())
        f\&.Close()
    }
}

.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp

